$QQ$ is countable:
$
  QQ = union.big_(n in NN) {(m)/(n) : m in ZZ}
$
is a countable union of countable sets.

Any family ${A_i : i in I}$ of pairwise disjoint open intervals in $RR$ is countable: those of length at least $1/n$ inject into the integer multiples of $1/n$, so $I = union.big_(n in NN) {i in I : "length of" A_i >= 1/n}$ is a countable union of countable sets. Alternatively, each interval contains a rational, and picking one gives an injection $I -> QQ$.
